# Build context hygiene for the multi-stage Dockerfiles.
#
# Why this file is required: every service Dockerfile does
#   1. COPY <Service>/<Service>.csproj   -> dotnet restore
#   2. COPY <Service>/                   -> dotnet build --no-restore
# Without this file, step 2 also copies the *host's* obj/ and bin/ folders on
# top of the ones the container just restored. A host-generated
# obj/project.assets.json points at the developer's absolute package folder
# (e.g. C:\Users\<user>\.nuget\packages), so the in-container build fails with
#   NETSDK1064: Package '<x>' was not found.
# Excluding them keeps the restore stage authoritative and makes local image
# builds behave exactly like a clean CI checkout.

**/bin/
**/obj/
**/TestResults/
**/node_modules/

# Local secrets must never be baked into an image. docker compose reads .env
# from the project directory for variable substitution, not from the build
# context, so excluding it changes nothing functionally.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Contains private SSH keys for the brokered JIT terminal.
jit-keys/
*.pem
*.key

# VCS / IDE
.git/
.gitignore
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
